 ## Meaning and origin
 
-又 means “again,” “also” or “or.” As a word, また means again, also, on the other hand, and, or or (JMdict entry 1524930), and 又は または means “or; either … or” (JMdict entry 1524990); JMdict notes that both are usually written in kana. JMdict entry 1524930 also has a prefix sense, “indirect,” and Digital Daijisen likewise says that また- attached to a noun marks something as indirect, as in [又聞き](../words/又聞き.md) and 又貸し.
+又 means “again,” “also” or “or.” As a word, [又](../words/また.md) また has senses that include “again,” “also,” “on the other hand,” “and; in addition” and “or; otherwise” (JMdict entry 1524930), and [又は](../words/または.md) または means “or; either … or” (JMdict entry 1524990). JMdict notes that both are usually written in kana, so the linked articles are headed in kana and show 又 and 又は as other spellings. JMdict entry 1524930 also has a prefix sense, “indirect,” and Digital Daijisen likewise says that また- attached to a noun marks something as indirect, as in 又聞き and 又貸し.
 
 ## Readings
 
 | Reading | Type | Typical words |
 | --- | --- | --- |
